WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:08.578
Your software library keeps releases ready for deployment. Let’s
publish a version; publishing alone won’t install it on any
device.

2
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.221
Choose Components to add a release to your software library.

3
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.858
Name the component and give this release a version number.

4
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.093
Choose the target platform and attach the matching software
file.

5
00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:25.895
Use Confidential for proprietary software. This demonstration
uses a public file.

6
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:33.295
Review the release, upload it, and approve the request in your
wallet. Keep the page open until publication finishes.

7
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:39.845
Look for the published version in your library. It is available
to deploy, but is not installed yet.

8
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:45.783
Your release is in the library. You’re ready to choose the
devices or groups that should receive it.
